Verdict: **CONCERNS / LEGIT**. The proof reconstructs cleanly, pins the real generated program, closes every claim, and rejects meaningful body/result mutations. The concern is the idealized unbounded-recursion semantics: actual CPython raises `RecursionError` on sufficiently long inputs, though this does not invalidate normal-return partial correctness.

